.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH PDFLUENT-EXTRACT 1  "pdfluent 1.1.0" PDFluent
.SH NAME
pdfluent\-extract \- Extract a document as Markdown, JSON, chunks, or text
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpdfluent extract\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-quality\fR] [\fB\-\-model\-dir\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-table\-model\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-pages\fR] [\fB\-\-images\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-recursive\fR] [\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-words\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUTS\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extract a document as Markdown, JSON, chunks, or text
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: md]
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
md: Markdown with headings, lists, and tables
.IP \(bu 2
json: Block\-model JSON (`to_json` over `extract_blocks`)
.IP \(bu 2
chunks: Docling JSON chunks for RAG ingestion
.IP \(bu 2
text: Plain text, one form feed per page
.IP \(bu 2
words: Every word with its box, one JSON object per line
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON envelope on stdout
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Quiet: human mode prints data only (no warnings or progress notes)
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fI<QUALITY>\fR [default: fast]
Extraction quality. `balanced` needs the `ort\-layout` build and the layout model (`pdfluent models install layout`)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fast: The shipping engine
.IP \(bu 2
balanced: The layout model tier; fails naming the install until it is there
.IP \(bu 2
best: Needs unshipped models; errors until they land
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-model\-dir\fR \fI<MODEL_DIR>\fR
Where the model tier looks for its weights. Default: the `PDFLUENT_MODEL_DIR` environment variable, else the per\-user model directory. Read only with `\-\-quality balanced`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose stderr diagnostics (repeat for more)
.TP
\fB\-\-table\-model\-dir\fR \fI<TABLE_MODEL_DIR>\fR
Where the TATR table model lives: `tatr\-v1.1\-all/tatr\-v1.1\-all.onnx` under this directory structures the balanced tier\*(Aqs kept table regions first (track B, P4). Needs the `ort\-tables` build; without it extraction refuses. Unset, `balanced` runs as it always has
.TP
\fB\-\-pages\fR \fI<PAGES>\fR
Pages to extract, e.g. `1\-3,5`. Default: the whole document
.TP
\fB\-\-images\fR \fI<IMAGES>\fR
What the Markdown carries for figures: `none` writes no reference, `embed` inlines each figure\*(Aqs pixels as a base64 data URL, and `dir:<path>` writes one PNG per figure and references it. Unset, references are markers naming the figure. With `dir:`, each input\*(Aqs files land in `<path>/<stem>/`, so batch inputs never share names
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Output file, directory, or `\-`/stdout. Directories are created. Multiple inputs need a directory
.TP
\fB\-\-recursive\fR
Descend into subdirectories (symlinks are never followed)
.TP
\fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<JOBS>\fR [default: 1]
Parallel inputs when writing files (stdout stays sequential)
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR
Keep going after a failed input. Default stops at the first error, keeping earlier outputs and cancelling the rest; with this every input is attempted, later successes are still written, and every error is reported (a re\-run then needs \-\-force for those)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing output files
.TP
\fB\-\-words\fR
Carry each block\*(Aqs word lines in the JSON output (`\-\-format json`). Without the flag the JSON is exactly what it was: no word lines
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUTS\fR>
Input PDFs, globs, directories, or `\-` for stdin (alone)
.SH VERSION
v1.1.0
